  "id": "knee-flexion",
  "name": "Knee Flexion",
  "definition": "A strict open-chain lever-machine isolation in which the lower leg flexes at the knee while the hip, pelvis, spine, ankle, and foot remain held. The roster owns four exact commercial-machine fixtures: unilateral seated and prone conditions plus a bilateral Johnson SL160 seated curl and a bilateral Flex Fitness prone curl. Hip angle, ankle posture, support, handles, and cadence remain fixture-specific and unreported fields are not invented. Standing curls, cable or band curls, Nordics, razor curls, glute-ham raises, sliding or ball curls, and hip-extension tasks remain outside this family.",
